      "problem": "It's known that there is a strong positive linear correlation between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine the given situation.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should be scattered *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/f918c0b1ec7a3b3969fef43eb60bba0b4d4afba813082d710c456d4c53a49018.png)",
